{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools on the two MCP servers.\n\nA timeout doesn't tell me whether the adjustment was recorded. I'll check for it before retrying so I don't ship twice.\n\nThe timed-out call had gone through, as `adj-107`. I'll ship the remaining claims and check by reference after any error.\n\n1106 hit a connection reset. I'll retry it with the same idempotency key, which returns the original result if the first call went through.\n\nNow the statuses.\n\nNext I'll check the 1106 comment, since that call had an error, and write the status file.\n\nI processed all 25 open warranty claims in ticket id order. Each claim has one comment and its status set. I ran no final check of every ticket and adjustment, only 1106's comment (one comment, correct) and the `adj-107` shipment. `/app/STATUS.json` is written with status `success`.\n\n- **Shipped (15, resolved):**\n  - **By me (14):** 1107, 1108, 1113, 1114, 1117, 1120, 1122, 1123, 1124, 1126, 1127, 1133, 1134 and 1135.\n  - **Before me (1):** 1125 was answered with the existing `adj-102`, and I shipped nothing more.\n  - **Successor sku:** 1127 shipped `PT-1219`, because `PT-1203` is discontinued.\n  - **Fallback warehouses:** 1133 shipped from north because west had run out after 1107. 1122 shipped from north, which held exactly 1 unit.\n- **Not covered (8, closed):**\n  - **Warranty expired:** 1106, 1110, 1115, 1116 and 1118.\n  - **Product line excluded:** 1121 and 1128.\n  - **Serial already replaced:** 1132, because 1103 already got `adj-24` for the same serial.\n- **Backordered (1, pending):** 1130 needs 2 units of `PT-1209`. East and west each hold only 1, so nothing shipped.\n- **Duplicate (1, duplicate):** 1131 has the same serial as 1108 and was answered as \"Duplicate of #1108.\"\n\nTwo calls failed with errors along the way. The `adjust_stock` call for 1107 timed out, but a check showed it had been recorded as `adj-107`, so I did not repeat it. The comment on 1106 hit a connection reset, and the retry with the same idempotency key left a single comment.\n\nI left the already-resolved or closed warranty tickets (1103, 1105), the pending 1112 and the policy tickets alone.","final_output":"I processed all 25 open warranty claims in ticket id order. Each claim has one comment and its status set. I ran no final check of every ticket and adjustment, only 1106's comment (one comment, correct) and the adj-107 shipment. /app/STATUS.json is written with status success.\n\n- Shipped (15, resolved):\n  - By me (14): 1107, 1108, 1113, 1114, 1117, 1120, 1122, 1123, 1124, 1126, 1127, 1133, 1134 and 1135.\n  - Before me (1): 1125 was answered with the existing adj-102, and I shipped nothing more.\n  - Successor sku: 1127 shipped PT-1219, because PT-1203 is discontinued.\n  - Fallback warehouses: 1133 shipped from north because west had run out after 1107. 1122 shipped from north, which held exactly 1 unit.\n- Not covered (8, closed):\n  - Warranty expired: 1106, 1110, 1115, 1116 and 1118.\n  - Product line excluded: 1121 and 1128.\n  - Serial already replaced: 1132, because 1103 already got adj-24 for the same serial.\n- Backordered (1, pending): 1130 needs 2 units of PT-1209. East and west each hold only 1, so nothing shipped.\n- Duplicate (1, duplicate): 1131 has the same serial as 1108 and was answered as \"Duplicate of #1108.\"\n\nTwo calls failed with errors along the way. The adjust_stock call for 1107 timed out, but a check showed it had been recorded as adj-107, so I did not repeat it. The comment on 1106 hit a connection reset, and the retry with the same idempotency key left a single comment.\n\nI left the already-resolved or closed warranty tickets (1103, 1105), the pending 1112 and the policy tickets alone.","exit_code":0,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","resolved_provider":"anthropic","session_id":"UG7SM-AuxsWI","steps":168,"tool_calls":[{"name":"capability_search","status":"success"},{"name":"capability_search","status":"success"},{"name":"m